  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="3517-3cfc-cdc6-60c1" name="Sumerian &amp; Akkadian (Chariot Wars) - List Notes" publicationId="513c-2d0a-024a-da5a" hidden="false">
      <description>SUMERIAN &amp; AKKADIAN ARMY LIST (Chariot Wars, pp.6-11), 2500 BC to 1800 BC.
Characters up to 25% of the army; the army must include at least one character to command it. The commander is the character with the highest Leadership, so a small army of 1,000 points can be commanded by a Senior Officer (Ensi or Shaknu) rather than a General (Lugal or King). Chariotry up to 25%. Infantry at least 25%. Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 25%.
Tactics: screen the army with skirmishing missile troops; advance massed spearmen with big shields; use onager chariots at the right moment on open ground, screened by javelinmen.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Sumerian &amp; Akkadian]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Standard composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
